#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""vp: one noun-verb command line over all of ViewPoint (Track P, Claude-written, stdlib only).

    vp <noun> <verb> [vp flags] [child flags...] [-- child args verbatim]

Contract (every call):
Taxonomy: vpops/1.1 (design/COMMANDS.md + design/MCP_TOOLS.json by lane ops-design), 88 commands.
  stdout  bounded human text (at most --tail lines, 240 chars each, secrets redacted), then ONE last
          line: the JSON receipt {"ok","code","rc","data","next"}. --json prints the receipt only.
  exit    = receipt rc, a closed class: 0 OK, 1 FAIL, 2 USAGE, 3 REFUSED, 4 CONFIRM_REQUIRED,
          5 NOT_FOUND, 6 BUSY, 7 STATE, 8 DEPENDENCY, 9 UPSTREAM, 124 TIMEOUT

vp flags: --dry-run  --confirm ID  --json  --impl ref|swarm  --tail N  --head N  --timeout-s S
          --detach  --allow-display D  --allow-hybrid  --foreign-ok JOB
Every verb wraps a real entry point (never a copy of its code); child flags pass through unchanged.
Child output is run through newton-py `sh` (spooled, bounded, sha256) and paged with `vp out read`.
`vp sys help` prints the whole verb table; `vp sys doctor` checks every entry point.
"""
